  {
    "id": "b1",
    "topic": "Маркетинг",
    "title": "What Is a Target Audience?",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Every business wants to sell its products. But who will buy them? This is the main question of marketing. The answer is the target audience.",
      "A target audience is a group of people who need your product. They have similar problems, interests and habits. For example, a fitness club in the city center wants young people who work in offices. They are busy, so they need short workouts before or after work.",
      "Why is this important? If you try to sell to everyone, you sell to no one. Your message becomes weak and boring. When you know your audience, you can speak their language. You can choose the right words, the right pictures and the right channels.",
      "How can you find your audience? First, look at your current customers. Who are they? How old are they? Where do they live? Second, ask them questions. Small surveys are cheap and useful. Third, check your competitors. Who do they talk to?",
      "Good marketers never stop learning about their audience. People change, and the market changes too. So update your research every few months."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "b2",
    "topic": "История",
    "title": "The Lost Phone",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Anna lives in a small flat near the river. Every morning she takes the bus to work. One Monday, the bus was very crowded. Anna was tired, and she was listening to music.",
      "When she got off the bus, she put her hand in her pocket. Her phone wasn't there! She felt cold. All her photos, contacts and work notes were on that phone.",
      "She ran back to the bus stop, but the bus was already gone. Anna didn't know what to do. Then she remembered the number of the bus company. She went into a café and asked the waiter for help. He kindly gave her his phone.",
      "A woman from the company answered. \"Don't worry,\" she said. \"The driver found a phone ten minutes ago. You can pick it up at the main station after five o'clock.\"",
      "In the evening, Anna got her phone back. The driver smiled and said, \"Be careful next time!\" Anna thanked him and bought him a coffee. Since that day, she always keeps her phone in her bag."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "b3",
    "topic": "Маркетинг",
    "title": "Why Reviews Matter",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Before people buy something online, they usually read reviews. A review is an opinion of a real customer. It can be good or bad.",
      "Reviews help new customers trust a brand. Imagine two shops sell the same shoes at the same price. The first shop has two hundred positive reviews. The second shop has none. Which one will you choose? Most people choose the first one.",
      "Bad reviews are not always a disaster. They show that the reviews are honest. What matters is how the company reacts. A polite and fast answer can turn an angry customer into a loyal one.",
      "How can a small business get more reviews? It is simple: ask. Send a short message after the purchase. Thank the customer and give a link. Some companies offer a small discount for a review, but be careful: in some countries this is against the rules.",
      "Remember: people trust other people more than advertising."
    ]
  }
]
